<title>Havenly Feature Roadmap</title>
<style>
:root {
  /*
     Layout: Modern professional dashboard style.
     Clean vertical separation with a refined slate-blue palette.
  */
  --bg: #f8fafc;
  --fg: #0f172a;
  --accent: #2563eb;
  --accent-soft: #dbeafe;
  --border: #e2e8f0;
  --text-muted: #64748b;
  --card-bg: #ffffff;

  /* Semantic colors */
  --high-priority: #ef4444;
  --med-priority: #f59e0b;
  --low-priority: #10b981;
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
    --bg: #0f172a;
    --fg: #f1f5f9;
    --accent: #60a5fa;
    --accent-soft: #1e3a8a;
    --border: #1e293b;
    --text-muted: #94a3b8;
    --card-bg: #1e293b;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
}

:root[data-theme="dark"] {
  --bg: #0f172a;
  --fg: #f1f5f9;
  --accent: #60a5fa;
  --accent-soft: #1e3a8a;
  --border: #1e293b;
  --text-muted: #94a3b8;
  --card-bg: #1e293b;
  color-scheme: dark;
}

body {
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--fg);
  font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  line-height: 1.5;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.container {
  max-width: 1100px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 40px 24px;
}

header {
  margin-bottom: 48px;
  text-align: center;
}

h1 {
  font-size: 2.5rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
  text-wrap: balance;
  color: var(--fg);
}

.subtitle {
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  max-width: 600px;
  margin: 0 auto;
}

.lifecycle-section {
  margin-bottom: 64px;
}

.lifecycle-title {
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  margin-bottom: 24px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
}

.lifecycle-title::before {
  content: '';
  width: 4px;
  height: 24px;
  background: var(--accent);
  border-radius: 2px;
}

.flow-diagram {
  background: var(--card-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 24px;
  margin-bottom: 32px;
  overflow-x: auto;
}

.role-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
  gap: 24px;
  margin-bottom: 64px;
}

.role-card {
  background: var(--card-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 16px;
  padding: 24px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}

.role-header {
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
  padding-bottom: 12px;
  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-soft);
  color: var(--accent);
}

.feature-item {
  padding: 16px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.feature-item:last-child {
  border-bottom: none;
}

.feature-meta {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}

.feature-name {
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 1rem;
}

.priority-badge {
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 2px 8px;
  border-radius: 99px;
  color: white;
}

.p-high { background: var(--high-priority); }
.p-medium { background: var(--med-priority); }
.p-low { background: var(--low-priority); }

.user-story {
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  color: var(--fg);
  margin-bottom: 8px;
  font-style: italic;
}

.tech-req {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  background: var(--bg);
  padding: 4px 8px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  display: inline-block;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}

.metric {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--accent);
  display: block;
}

.mermaid {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
}
</style>

<div class="container">
  <header>
    <h1>Havenly Feature Roadmap</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A structured path toward financial transparency and formalized property maintenance for Tenants, Caretakers, and Admins.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="lifecycle-section">
    <div class="lifecycle-title">Core System Lifecycles</div>

    <div class="flow-diagram">
      <p style="font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--text-muted)">The Ticket Lifecycle</p>
      <pre class="mermaid">
        graph LR
          T[Tenant raises ticket] --> C[Caretaker manages/updates]
          C --> A[Admin oversees/approves]
          A --> C2[Caretaker resolves]
          C2 --> TN[Tenant notified]
          style T fill:var(--accent-soft),stroke:var(--accent)
          style TN fill:var(--accent-soft),stroke:var(--accent)
      </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="flow-diagram">
      <p style="font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--text-muted)">The Payment Lifecycle</p>
      <pre class="mermaid">
        graph LR
          P[Paystack trigger] --> L[Automatic ledger update]
          L --> H[Tenant history updated]
          style P fill:var(--accent-soft),stroke:var(--accent)
          style H fill:var(--accent-soft),stroke:var(--accent)
      </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="flow-diagram">
      <p style="font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--text-muted)">The Utility Lifecycle</p>
      <pre class="mermaid">
        graph LR
          C[Caretaker enters price] --> B[Bill generated/recorded]
          B --> TN[Tenant notified]
          style C fill:var(--accent-soft),stroke:var(--accent)
          style TN fill:var(--accent-soft),stroke:var(--accent)
      </pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="role-grid">
    <!-- CARETAKER -->
    <div class="role-card">
      <div class="role-header">Caretaker</div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Utility Price Entry</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-high">High</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As a caretaker, I want to enter utility prices for occupied houses so that bills are accurately recorded.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">RBAC: Write access restricted to OCCUPIED units</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: 100% of occupied units billed monthly.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Ticket Management</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-high">High</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As a caretaker, I want to update ticket status (Reported &rarr; In Progress &rarr; Resolved) to avoid word-of-mouth failures.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">Status State Machine + Notification Trigger</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: Reduction in duplicate reports.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Admin Escalation</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-medium">Medium</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As a caretaker, I want to forward tickets to the admin so that complex repairs get approved funding.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">Ticket Assignment Transfer logic</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: Average time to Admin approval.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- TENANT -->
    <div class="role-card">
      <div class="role-header">Tenant</div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Maintenance Portal</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-high">High</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As a tenant, I want to raise maintenance tickets via a formalized channel so that I have a record of my request.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">Ticket creation API + File upload for photos</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: % of tickets raised via portal vs phone.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Financial Ledger</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-medium">Medium</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As a tenant, I want to view my rent and utility payment history so that I have full financial transparency.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">Read-only Ledger View + Paystack Webhook sync</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: Decrease in billing disputes.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Utility Notifications</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-low">Low</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As a tenant, I want to be notified when a new utility bill is generated so I can pay it promptly.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">Push notifications / Email trigger on Bill creation</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: Average time from bill to payment.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ADMIN / LANDLORD -->
    <div class="role-card">
      <div class="role-header">Admin / Landlord</div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Automated Ledger Sync</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-high">High</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As an admin, I want payments to automatically update the ledger so that I don't have to manually reconcile Paystack logs.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">Paystack Integration + Idempotent ledger updates</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: Zero manual entries for Paystack payments.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Ticket Oversight</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-medium">Medium</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As an admin, I want to oversee and approve escalated tickets so that maintenance quality is maintained.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">Admin Approval Workflow + Notification system</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: Resolution rate of escalated tickets.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-item">
        <div class="feature-meta">
          <span class="feature-name">Manual Payment Recording</span>
          <span class="priority-badge p-medium">Medium</span>
        </div>
        <div class="user-story">As an admin, I want to manually record external payments so that the ledger remains the single source of truth.</div>
        <div class="tech-req">Admin-only Ledger Write access</div>
        <span class="metric">Success: Ledger accuracy vs bank statements.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
